1. under natural light, the electroplating products are placed at about 45 degrees of human visual angle to see whether the overall color is uniform and consistent, especially for some concave corners and holes, there can be no color difference. There should be no scratches, scratches and other phenomena.
If it is a non wipe stain, or obvious water stain, watermark, it cannot be selected. Another situation is that the edge corner will appear in the plating color is dim and lustrous, there are gray fog or white fog like spots, the hand feeling is not smooth, and can not be selected.
4. see if the adhesion of the surface of the electroplated coating is firm. The coating surface can be pasted with adhesive paper, and then torn at a 45 degree angle, and there should be no coating falling off.
