Shot blasting is a method used to clean, strengthen or polish metal, which is a technological process of removing various impurities from different surfaces by using the abrasive. It is an important process of surface protection and also prior-preparation of surfaces prior to further processing, such as welding, coloring, etc.
Sandblasting or bead blasting is a generic term for the process of smoothing, shaping and cleaning a hard surface by forcing solid particles across that surface at high speeds; the effect is similar to that of using sandpaper, but provides a more even finish with no problems at corners or crannies. Sandblasting can occur naturally, usually as a result of particles blown by wind causing aeolian erosion, or artificially, using compressed air.
