A bitcoin debit card is a VISA or Mastercard that you can use to buy goods and services from online and offline shops or withdraw money from ATMs.
The plastic bitcoin debit card looks like an ordinary VISA or Mastercard which you can use the same way.
The cardholder name, date of expiry and the CVC/CVV codes are provided upon order, but there is no phsyical production making it easier and faster to access the funds.
What are the currencies I can use a bitcoin debit card with?
In order to have a bitcoin debit card, you must register at one of the providers’ platform.
If you do not want to share personal information, you can order an anonymous bitcoin debit card without verification.
If you do not want to go through the verification process of providing photo ID and proof of residence, you can choose an anonymous bitcoin debit card.
Therefore only limited amount of funds can be used with the anonymous bitcoin debit cards in exchange for only providing a name to be displayed on the card.
The plastic bitcoin debit cards are issued by VISA or Mastercard and it takes about 2-3 weeks to receive them.
In most cases however PayPal is not among the accepted withdrawal method for bitcoin debit cards.
Beside the one time production cost of the card, a monthly account maintenance fee is charged in the amount of 1 USD per month.
The transaction costs of the bitcoin debit cards are varying widely, the more expensive cards can have smaller transaction fees.
The POS and online purchased can be charged with a fixed fee or at a prorata percentage.
In some cases there is maximum amount of fund you can load to a bitcoin debit card.
Verified users may have higher limits and also some providers offers unlimited bitcoin debit card for registered users.
What are the ATM withdrawal fees associated with a bitcoin debit card?
This fee can be charged per transaction or prorata.
What is currency translation fee associated with bitcoin debit card transactions?
In this case a fixed 3% currency translation fee is charged by all of the providers on the market.
Users can benefit from the advantages of the bitcoin network while streamlining currency translations and hedging against market movements.
The VISA debit card issued by the company is backed with bitcoin amounts that people can use up in online purchases or withdrawals from ATMs.
After connecting the bank account to the platform, users can convert EUR, GBP or USD amounts into bitcoins.
The cards are accepted at all POS terminals where VISA cards are accepted.
Besides the traditional VISA cards that have chips and pins, users can also order virtual cards, which are accepted as widely as the plastic cards.
Bank accounts eligible within the 28 SEPA countries in Europe, but cards can be ordered outside of the Eurozone too.
Besides the United States, the company excludes an additional 120 countries from their services, including couple of countries in Africa and in the Middle-East.
After the order is made through the website, customer receives the debit card within 2-3 weeks in Europe and 3-5 weeks in the rest of the word.
The plastic cards allow verified users to withdraw daily 2,000 USD from ATMs and there is 10,000 USD limit on single top ups.
Cryptopay offers it’s user base the option to use its services without verification too.
Unverified users may withdraw 400 USD daily from ATMs, but only in a total amount of 1,000 USD throughout the lifetime of the access.
On the other side, both type of users may use Cryptopay debit cards unlimited time for online purchases.
The cheapest way is to load the account balance with the on-site Cryptopay loading tool, because otherwise the platform charges an additional 0.99% for using third-party services.
Users must pay attention to the base currency of the Cryptopay card as there is an additional 3% charge on foreign transactions.
The fee of ATM withdrawals for domestic and international transactions in euros are the same € 2.25.
The bitcoin prices are not traded at much premium and the bid/offer margin is reasonable.
There are a number of fees that are applicable for utilizing and loading Cryptopay debit card.
The registration only takes one minute.
Verification takes just a few hours.
The balances can be withdrawn to another bitcoin wallet or to linked bank accounts under Send section.
In case any question arise, there is a search function in the FAQ section.
The only negative feedback mentioned was that the customer support works in UK time zone only that could be a headache for overseas clients.
The website is built well designed.
Spectrocoin combined technological reliability with infrastructural comprehensiveness in order to create a high-quality bitcoin service for its clients.
The company also provides a solution for merchant so they can accept bitcoin through their business activities.
Both the plastic and the virtual cards are accepted at the more than 20 million sites and online shops across the internet.
Spectrocoin offers company cards as a solution for those who are one step ahead in the digital world.
Normal shipping if free and the card arrives in 3-4 weeks.
And who would t need that?
The service uses two factor authorization for login.
In order to verify the users themselves, they must provide a valid passport or ID card and a utility bill.
If any funds is received by an unverified card, these funds are blocked until the card is being verified.
Total ATM withdrawal limit for unverified users is 1000 USD.
Justas Dobiliauskas is the chief technology officer at the startup due to his 6+ years experience s a developer at enterprise software designing companies.
However this fee is not charged if the balance of the account is zero.
Loading costs of the cards are free if the funds are coming from a Spectrocoin account.
When using ATMs, Spectrocoin charges 2.5 USD for domestic currency withdrawal and 3.5 USD for other currency withdrawal.
When receiving funds to the card, the POS load fee is 1.99%.
Spectrocoin website although provides a lot of information on the services, still does not include everything handy that a possible future user may need.
These information alone doesn’t seem too important, but when a user is looking for something and cannot find, it can be frustrating.
Spectrocoin by so far have not defended themselves on these charges.
