There are 3 reasons for the high pressure of the auto air conditioning system:
When the cooling fan of the water tank fails, the air conditioner is still used for a long time and with high intensity (the cooling fan of the water tank is shared with the air conditioning condenser fan);
In order to avoid such failures, the car air conditioner should not be used in the following 3 situations.
When the amount of refrigerant added exceeds the regulation, it must be discharged in time, otherwise, the air conditioner is not allowed to be used. The method to check the amount of refrigerant is: when the car ac compressor starts to work, check whether there are bubbles in the observation window of the liquid storage tank.
When the cooling fan of the water tank fails and stops running, the air conditioner should be stopped immediately, otherwise, the refrigeration system will generate ultra-high pressure, which will cause the electromagnetic clutch to slip and burn.
When parking, when the engine is idling, it is best not to turn on the air conditioner.
Disconnect the connector on your compressor's magnetic coil. Use the right size socket to remove the 6 mm bolt in the center of the AC clutch.
They are used to gap the clutch properly, so keep them in a safe place to avoid losing them. Remove the snap-ring on the shaft that secures the pulley, and slide this off the shaft.
Clean the shaft and other parts thoroughly before installation. Insert the new pulley, and engage the snap-ring with the beveled edge facing outward.
Place the feeler gauge between the clutch and the pulley to ensure proper clearance. If the clearance is not correct, remove the clutch plate and add another spacer.
Although mechanical control valves still function in older and more economical cars due to the additional cost, the control range of electronic control valves is much superior. The electronic control valve is more efficient and reduces the displacement, reduces the wear of the AC system, reduces the engine load during operation, and produces cleaner emissions.
During periods of medium and high A/C demand, the system suction pressure will be greater than the control valve set point. During these periods, the control valve maintains bleed air from the crankcase to the suction port.
During periods of low to medium A/C demand, the system suction pressure will drop to the control valve set point. The control valve maintains the exhaust from the exhaust to the crankcase and prevents the exhaust from the crankcase to the intake.
