The Spheripol double-loop gas phase polypropylene technology developed and put into operation by basell is the most experienced new type of polypropylene synthesis process. Compared with the traditional production process, the produced polypropylene products have better quality and larger output.
Prior to this, all polypropylene synthesis processes controlled the reaction temperature at about 70°C to avoid the generation of bubbles during the production process and make the polypropylene products more homogeneous. The Borstar process designed by Borealis allows a higher operating temperature, which can even exceed the critical value of propylene operation.
