The SMS service is used for collecting and disseminating price information for fruit and vegetables (we are currently expanding it to other products), sold by whole sale traders in 16 markets from around Cambodia. The SMS service is currently focused on fruit and vegetables.
The prices from the government data collectors are average prices in the market and collected three times a week. Where as prices from the traders are received on a daily basis, normally during the early trading hours of the day.
Traders who have registered with our SMS service, can submit the selling price for a commodity, this can only be done from the phone number with which they have registered. Traders are registered by market and therefore do not need to indicate the market code when submitting a price.
