Mu Sochua, a self-exiled former deputy president of the CNRP, said in a message that “the cancellation of Sar Kheng’s visit is telling and significant of Germany’s stance for democracy and role among EU members that have pursue sanctions and speaking with one voice”.
One of them was Sochua, who said she had met with the head of the Foreign Ministry’s Asia Department in October.
